<title>USA: Gingrich hopes for disaster bill passage today.</title>
<headline>Gingrich hopes for disaster bill passage today.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>House Speaker Newt Gingrich said Thursday he hoped to reach a compromise on disaster assistance legislation with Democrats and the Senate that would allow passage of the bill later in the day.</p>
<p>The Georgia Republican informed the House that discussions were continuing on legislation that would involve passage of somewhat less than the full $8.6 billion originally approved for disaster relief, military operations and other non-emergency government activities.</p>
<p>He spoke on the House floor.</p>
</text>
